  "parsed_answer": "Yes. **SRD5A2** encodes **5\u03b1-reductase type 2**, the enzyme targeted by several **androgenetic hair loss** treatments.\n\nThe integrated evidence commonly links SRD5A2 to:\n\n- **Finasteride** \u2014 a **5\u03b1-reductase inhibitor** used for male pattern hair loss.\n- **Dutasteride** \u2014 another **5\u03b1-reductase inhibitor** that inhibits both type 1 and type 2 enzymes and has also been investigated for hair loss.\n\nSo, the main treatment class linked to SRD5A2 is **5\u03b1-reductase inhibition**, especially **finasteride** and **dutasteride**.",
